    "body": "## Background\n\nDecode engines in disaggregated serving admit prefilled requests through `add_request_with_kv_handoff()`. The inference review found two gaps:\n- `InferenceClient.add_request_with_kv_handoff()` accepts a string or a token list and forwards a string unchanged. The decode side called `torch.tensor()` on the prompt, so a string prompt raised inside the engine loop.\n- Unlike `SUBMIT_REQUEST`, the `SUBMIT_REQUEST_WITH_KV` handler in `schedule_requests()` had no `try/except`. That error, or any other handoff validation error, escaped the loop and the client never got a reply.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `inference_state_handoff.py`: `prompt` is typed `str | list[int]`. A string prompt is tokenized once with `controller.tokenize_prompt(tokenizer, prompt, sampling_params.add_BOS)` before block hashing. The deferred and pending import records and the finalizer's `add_request()` then all carry the same token IDs.\n- `dynamic_engine.py`: the `SUBMIT_REQUEST_WITH_KV` handler wraps `add_request_with_kv_handoff()` and sends any exception to `_fail_submission()`. That registers the same FAILED placeholder the plain submit path already uses. The `_fail_submission` docstring now mentions this caller.\n- New tests: `test_schedule_requests_fails_a_rejected_kv_handoff_and_continues` in `test_dynamic_engine.py` and `test_string_handoff_prompt_is_tokenized_once_before_import` in `test_disagg_handoff_lifecycle.py`.\n\n## Details\n\nEvery MP rank processes the same broadcast message, so the failure path keeps request state mirrored across ranks. One behavior change: a non-disaggregated engine that receives `SUBMIT_REQUEST_WITH_KV` now fails that one request with a reply instead of raising out of the loop. This was split out of the inference review. It is independent of #8255, which handles replying to a failed KV import.\n\n## Tested\n\n- black, isort, pylint (10.00/10) and ruff are clean on the 4 changed files.\n- Run on 8×H100 at this head merged with main `3914483f`, using main's CI image (`sha256:7b4e22a3`):\n  - `tests/unit_tests/inference/**/*.py`: 3675 passed, 37 skipped, 0 failed.\n  - `tests/unit_tests/inference/engines/test_dynamic_engine.py`: 254 passed, 2 skipped.\n- No functional test case exercises disaggregation.",
    "changed_files": 4,
